    "narrative": "Today\u2019s offensive engine for the Austin Waves relies heavily on the platoon-advantaged upside against Andrew Abbott. **Miguel Vargas** leads our lineup with a 63.53 efficiency score; his ability to exploit the lefty-on-lefty matchup with strong xwOBA metrics makes him our anchor. **Kyle Tucker** (60.78) and **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** (60.95) provide high-floor consistency, though **Vladimir Guerrero Jr.** faces a challenging outing against the 3.31 xERA of Tolle. While we remain cautious of the skill gap, the order placement for both **Kyle Tucker** and **Miguel Vargas** keeps their counting stat projections elevated, which is vital as we fight to maintain our standing in the competitive Roto landscape.\n\nThe optimization process required a tough call at the margins, particularly concerning **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, who scored a robust 58.88. His dynamic platoon advantage against Logan Gilbert provided enough runway to earn a UTIL start over other peripheral options. **Wade Meckler** (42.25) remains in the lineup despite the grim prospect of facing the elite arm of Jacob deGrom; his role as a leadoff hitter and his elite sprint speed\u2014a necessity given our focus on the scarce SB category\u2014compel us to play him regardless of the SP_xERA hurdle. \n\nRegarding risks, nearly half of our outfield is currently listed as \"Lineup Pending,\" which introduces volatility into our efficiency scores. We are particularly monitoring **Nasim Nunez** (51.96); while his raw hitting metrics are pedestrian, the combination of his speed profile and the slow delivery of Kevin Gausman creates a hidden floor for stolen base potential that outweighs the risk of his #9 spot in the order. We are continuing to monitor the health of **Jordan Westburg**, whose IL status remains the primary bottleneck for our internal roster flexibility alongside the current off-days for **Gunnar Henderson**, **Luis Robert Jr.**, and **Jackson Merrill**. Should the lineups for **Andy Pages**, **Luis Lara**, or **Wade Meckler** shift, we are prepared to pivot to our depth, including **Jacob Wilson**, **Drake Baldwin**, or **Heliot Ramos**, to ensure we hit our daily game caps efficiently.",
